From: A6L ADSP research (claude-adsp) <none@localhost>
Subject: [CANDIDATE B, NOT BUILT, NOT TESTED] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_pas: Hisense A6L stock-style LPASS CX proxy vote

Only for use if candidate A ("qcom,sdm660-adsp-pas", no proxy vote) times out
waiting for the ADSP ready signal ("start timed out", qcom_q6v5_wait_for_start
returns -ETIMEDOUT after 5 s) or the ADSP reports an early fatal error.

Evidence for the difference (see research/claude-adsp/EVIDENCE.md, D5):
  * stock DTB (firmware/extracted/device-trees/stock-00.dts, node
    qcom,lpass@15700000): vdd_cx-supply = <&pm660l_l9_level>,
    qcom,vdd_cx-uV-uA = <0x180 0x186a0>  => RPM resource "rwlc"/0
    (LPASS/SSC CX, PM660L L9 in level mode) proxied at level 384 (TURBO),
    load 100000 uA, both RPM sets, released on the proxy-unvote smp2p bit.
  * pinned driver: adsp_resource_init has no proxy_pd_names, so the single
    "cx" power domain (rpmpd RPMPD_VDDCX = RPM "rwcx"/0) is only attached by
    the platform core; no performance level is ever voted on rwlc/0.

This candidate adds a vendor match that:
  * uses proxy_pd_names = {"cx"} so qcom_pas_pds_attach() takes the
    single-domain path (devs[0] = dev, pm_runtime_enable) and qcom_pas_start()
    votes dev_pm_genpd_set_performance_state(dev, INT_MAX) -> rpmpd clamps to
    max_state = RPM_SMD_LEVEL_TURBO (384), exactly the stock level, released
    at handover (qcom_pas_handover -> qcom_pas_pds_disable);
  * sets auto_boot = false so the diagnostic controls the start explicitly.
The companion overlay a6l-adsp-diag-ssccx.dtso points power-domains at
<&rpmpd RPMPD_SSCCX> (RPM "rwlc"/0, dt-bindings/power/qcom-rpmpd.h value 6)
so the vote lands on the same RPM resource as stock.

Base: sdm660-mainline/linux e47d622cb6d2440a9eacdc8bb2df32c037bec7b8 (7.2.3)
File: drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c (adsp_resource_init at lines 900-908,
      of_match entry "qcom,sdm660-adsp-pas" at line 1613 of that revision).
Rebuild only the qcom_q6v5_pas module in an isolated copy of the validated
output directory, exactly as tools/Prepare-HapticBrakeFix.py did for the
haptics module; vermagic must stay "7.2.3-a6l-probe+ SMP preempt mod_unload
aarch64" and the Image/Module.symvers must remain unchanged.
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -907,6 +907,27 @@ static const struct qcom_pas_data adsp_resource_init = {
 	.ssctl_id = 0x14,
 };
 
+/*
+ * Hisense A6L (HLTE730T, SDM660): the stock pil-tz-generic node proxies the
+ * LPASS CX rail (RPM "rwlc"/0 via pm660l_l9_level) at TURBO until the ADSP
+ * signals proxy-unvote. Vote the single "cx" power domain (pointed at
+ * RPMPD_SSCCX by the board DT) at its maximum level during boot and release
+ * it at handover. Manual start only, for bounded diagnostics.
+ */
+static const struct qcom_pas_data a6l_adsp_proxycx_resource = {
+	.crash_reason_smem = 423,
+	.firmware_name = "adsp.mdt",
+	.pas_id = 1,
+	.auto_boot = false,
+	.proxy_pd_names = (char*[]){
+		"cx",
+		NULL
+	},
+	.ssr_name = "lpass",
+	.sysmon_name = "adsp",
+	.ssctl_id = 0x14,
+};
+
 static const struct qcom_pas_data sa8775p_adsp_resource = {
 	.crash_reason_smem = 423,
 	.firmware_name = "adsp.mbn",
@@ -1577,6 +1598,7 @@ static const struct qcom_pas_data x1e80100_cdsp_resource = {
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id qcom_pas_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "hisense,a6l-adsp-pas", .data = &a6l_adsp_proxycx_resource },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,eliza-adsp-pas", .data = &sm8550_adsp_resource },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,milos-adsp-pas", .data = &sm8550_adsp_resource },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,milos-cdsp-pas", .data = &milos_cdsp_resource },
--
